---
import Mascot from '../components/Mascot.astro';
import { INDEXABLE } from '../site';
import pkg from '../../../packages/fnclaude/package.json';
import '../styles/landing.css';

// The header version is the umbrella package's, read at build time so a
// release bump propagates without anyone editing this page.
const { version } = pkg;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>fnclaude</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Session control for Claude Code: move a running session to another repository, or open a sibling beside it, each starting from a written continuity summary."
    />
    {!INDEXABLE && <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />}
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;0,800;1,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&display=swap"
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="session-head wrap">
      <Mascot class="rhombus" />

      <div class="head-lines">
        <h1 class="head-name">fnclaude<span class="ver">v{version}</span></h1>
        <div class="head-meta">
          Session control for Claude Code &middot; <span class="on">fnc</span> for short
        </div>
        <div class="head-meta">~/src/fnclaude@fnclaude</div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero wrap">
        <h1>Start a session <em>anywhere.</em> Move it mid-flight.</h1>

        <p>
          Claude Code starts in the directory you are standing in and stays there.
          <span class="lit">fnclaude</span> takes a repo reference instead &mdash; a short
          name, an <span class="lit">owner/name</span>, a URL &mdash; finds it or clones it,
          and launches there. Once you are in, it hands the session tools to move itself.
        </p>

        <div class="prompt">
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
          <code>npm i -g fnclaude</code>
          <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>

        <p class="hint">
          Then <kbd>fnc</kbd> anywhere &mdash; or <kbd>fnc &lt;repo&gt;</kbd> to start somewhere
          specific.
        </p>

        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started/">Get Started</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/fnclaude/fnclaude">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="transcript wrap">
        <h2 class="section-label">Launching</h2>

        <dl class="calls">
          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc ~/src/proj</dt>
            <dd>
              Not bound to where you are. Pass any directory and the session starts there,
              from whatever terminal you happen to have open.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc arch-setup</dt>
            <dd>
              A bare name is enough. fnclaude looks for a matching clone on disk, and if
              there isn&rsquo;t one, searches your GitHub organisations and clones it.
              <span class="note">You type the short name. It finds the thing.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc fnrhombus/arch-setup</dt>
            <dd>
              Qualify it when you want to skip the search: <code>name@owner</code>,
              <code>owner/name</code>, <code>gh:owner/name</code>, an HTTPS URL, or an SSH
              URL. All resolve to the same clone destination.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc opus max</dt>
            <dd>
              Model and effort are bare words in the first two slots, not flags with
              spelled-out values. <code>opus</code>, <code>sonnet</code>,
              <code>haiku</code>, <code>fable</code>; <code>low</code> through
              <code>max</code>.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc high ~/src/proj</dt>
            <dd>
              An effort level on its own implies <code>opus</code>, because that is the
              only reason you were reaching for it.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc resume</dt>
            <dd>
              Picking up where you left off is one word. <code>continue</code> takes the
              most recent session, <code>fork</code> branches off one. Short forms:
              <code>res</code>, <code>con</code>, <code>fk</code>.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc resume ~/src/proj</dt>
            <dd>
              The picker, scoped to a project you are not currently in. Resume a session
              somewhere else without going there first.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc resume &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; Ctrl-A</dt>
            <dd>
              In the picker, <kbd>Ctrl-A</kbd> widens the list to sessions from every
              directory. Choose one from another project and fnclaude relaunches itself
              there, carrying every flag from the original invocation.
              <span class="note">Plain claude prints the cd-and-resume line and leaves you to run it.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc arch-setup+fix-lid-sync</dt>
            <dd>
              A <code>+</code> suffix resolves the base repo and adds a worktree beside it,
              branched and ready.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc -w fix-lid-sync</dt>
            <dd>
              Names an existing worktree and fnclaude swaps its cwd to it. Names a new one
              and it passes through as a create request.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div class="call">
            <dt>fnc -BVC</dt>
            <dd>
              A capital letter per claude long flag, collapsing the POSIX way. That one is
              <code>--brief --verbose --chrome</code>.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="transcript wrap">
        <h2 class="section-label">Once you are in a session</h2>

        <div class="exchanges">
          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">switch me over to arch-setup</p>
            <p class="tool">fnc_switch_project</p>
            <p class="said">
              Ends this session and re-launches at the destination, carrying a written
              continuity summary so the new one opens knowing what it is there for. You get
              a few seconds to <kbd>Ctrl-C</kbd> out of it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">also open a session for fncode</p>
            <p class="tool">fnc_spawn_session</p>
            <p class="said">
              Opens a sibling in a new terminal window and leaves this session running. Two
              tracks in parallel, neither waiting on the other.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">restart yourself</p>
            <p class="tool">fnc_restart</p>
            <p class="said">
              Restarts in place with the conversation intact and your original flags
              preserved. Name a flag to change and only that one changes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">what&rsquo;s this session cost so far?</p>
            <p class="tool">get_usage</p>
            <p class="said">
              Cost, a per-model token breakdown, and the live context size &mdash; read from
              data fnclaude already holds. No extra API calls to ask.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">drop to sonnet for the rest of this</p>
            <p class="tool">fnc_set_model</p>
            <p class="said">
              Changes the model on the running session. No restart, no losing the thread.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">crank the effort up to max</p>
            <p class="tool">fnc_set_effort</p>
            <p class="said">
              Same, for reasoning effort: <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>,
              <code>high</code>, <code>xhigh</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>auto</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exchange">
            <p class="ask">put that command on my clipboard</p>
            <p class="tool">fnc_copy_to_clipboard</p>
            <p class="said">
              Hands you text without a round trip through select-and-copy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="outro">
          <span>MIT licensed</span>
          <span>Linux and macOS</span>
          <a href="/installation/">Installation</a>
          <a href="/reference/tools/">Tool reference</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="statusbar">
      <div class="status-left">
        <span class="perm"
          >&#9656;&#9656; bypass permissions on <span class="muted">(shift+tab to cycle)</span
          ></span
        >
      </div>

      <div class="status-right">
        <div class="burndowns" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="burn">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 44 16"
              ><g fill="#6d6d6d">
                <rect x="2" y="3" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="7" y="4" width="1" height="1" />
                <rect x="12" y="6" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="17" y="7" width="1" height="1" />
                <rect x="22" y="9" width="1" height="1" /><rect
                  x="27"
                  y="10"
                  width="1"
                  height="1"
                />
                <rect x="32" y="12" width="1" height="1" /><rect
                  x="37"
                  y="13"
                  width="1"
                  height="1"
                />
              </g></svg
            >
            <span>5h</span>
          </div>
          <div class="burn">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 44 16">
              <rect x="2" y="2" width="1" height="1" fill="#c9b458" />
              <g fill="#6d6d6d">
                <rect x="7" y="4" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="12" y="5" width="1" height="1" />
                <rect x="17" y="7" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="22" y="8" width="1" height="1" />
                <rect x="27" y="10" width="1" height="1" /><rect
                  x="32"
                  y="11"
                  width="1"
                  height="1"
                />
                <rect x="37" y="13" width="1" height="1" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <span>7d</span>
          </div>
          <div class="burn">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 44 16">
              <rect x="2" y="3" width="1" height="1" fill="#b7bdf7" />
              <g fill="#6d6d6d">
                <rect x="7" y="5" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="12" y="6" width="1" height="1" />
                <rect x="17" y="8" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="22" y="9" width="1" height="1" />
                <rect x="27" y="11" width="1" height="1" /><rect
                  x="32"
                  y="12"
                  width="1"
                  height="1"
                />
                <rect x="37" y="13" width="1" height="1" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <span>opus</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <span class="model">Opus 5 <span class="eff">high</span></span>
        <span class="rc">/rc</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
